A||||5||dnixon||87 GT starting problems||||
Z||000000||dnixon||08-31-99||11:58 PM||||Help!!<p>About once every six weeks my 87 GT 2.8 V6 with 135k refuses to start.   The next morning it starts fine.   There is no consistency to this.   Tonight it started, ran for about a second, then cut out.   I had to abandon it.  I left it with GM mechanics once for a whole week, but they couldn't reproduce the fault.   Battery, plugs, fuel pump all seem ok.   Maybe it's Y2K.<p>Has anyone any similar experience and/or a suggestion for a cure?<p>Love the car, but it's so unreliable in this I daren't go anywhere in it. 
Z||000001||DJRice||09-01-99||07:25 AM||||You should check the wires at your distribuion block mounted near the battery.  One could be loose.  When that happens, nothing in the car will work.
Z||000002||dnixon||09-04-99||09:54 PM||||To DJRice<p>Thanks for the response.   I missed it before.   I tried waggling those connectors to no effect.   Can't understand, either, why it would be ok in the morning, with no other action, and with ambient conditions similar.   Every time we try diagnostics it's ok.   Maybe a bad joint in the module, or a lazy chip.   Maybe I'll have to wait till it packs up completely.<p>Thanks for calling.
Z||000003||K9||09-05-99||05:54 PM||||I had a simmler problem with my 85 GT. while driveing it would just stop working, and then it woulden't start for about a day.I checked everythig but coulden't find the problem.The problem would occure randomly and under any driving conductions.I thought it was a lost cause.One day I started the car and with the car running I check all the electrical connection.Wiggleing it, pulling on it, and shaking it while listing to the engine idle.I came across a louse cannection between the distubuter and the coil.After fixing the connection at the distubuter the problem no longer remains.Try the same thing anb see if you get anywhere. 
Z||000004||Dave85||09-05-99||06:26 PM||||That is the same problem my car had before I bought it. It finally died for good. I bought the car for $500 and $35 later, for a new ignition module, it's still running great.  
Z||000005||dnixon||09-08-1999||12:27 AM||||Thanks everybody.   Actually looks like it might be in the distributor.   It's starting to break up - and that after being installed only 30,000 km.||||reg||
